{"id":"mahabharata-9-040","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":40,"title":"चत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 40 · Baka Dalbhya and the Saraswati's tirthas","summary":{"en":"Balarama comes to the place where the sage Baka Dalbhya performed a sacrifice with the flesh of the king's cattle and made the king's realm fall. He then passes on to the tirthas of the Saraswati, where the god Skanda received his command.","kn":"ಬಲರಾಮ ಬಕ ದಾಲ್ಭ್ಯ ರಾಜನ ಪಶುಗಳ ಮಾಂಸದಿಂದ ಯಜ್ಞ ಮಾಡಿ ರಾಜ್ಯ ಪತನ ಮಾಡಿದ ಸ್ಥಳಕ್ಕೆ ಬರುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಂತರ ಸ್ಕಂದ ಸೇನಾಪತ್ಯ ಪಡೆದ ಸರಸ್ವತಿ ತೀರ್ಥಗಳನ್ನು ದಾಟುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"बलराम उस स्थान पर आते हैं जहाँ ऋषि बक दाल्भ्य ने राजा के पशुओं के मांस से यज्ञ किया और राजा का राज्य गिरा दिया। फिर वे सरस्वती के उन तीर्थों से गुजरते हैं जहाँ स्कन्द को सेनापतित्व मिला।","te":"బలరాముడు బక దాల్భ్యుడు రాజు పశువుల మాంసంతో యజ్ఞం చేసి రాజ్యాన్ని పతనం చేసిన చోటుకు వస్తాడు. తరువాత స్కందునికి సేనాపత్యం లభించిన సరస్వతీ తీర్థాలను దాటుతాడు.","ta":"பலராமன் முனிவர் பகன் தால்ப்யன் அரசனின் பசுக்களின் ஊனால் வேள்வி செய்து அரசு வீழச்செய்த இடத்துக்கு வருகிறான். பின் ஸ்கந்தன் படைத்தலைமை பெற்ற சரஸ்வதி தீர்த்தங்களைக் கடக்கிறான்.","ml":"ബലരാമൻ ബകദാൽഭ്യൻ എന്ന ഋഷി രാജാവിന്റെ പശുക്കളുടെ മാംസംകൊണ്ട് യജ്ഞം ചെയ്ത് രാജ്യം നശിപ്പിച്ച സ്ഥലത്തെത്തുന്നു. തുടർന്ന് സ്കന്ദന് ആജ്ഞ ലഭിച്ച സരസ്വതി തീർത്ഥങ്ങളിലേക്ക് അദ്ദേഹം പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.40; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"सारस्वतपर्व","titleEn":"Sarasvata Parva (Balarama's pilgrimage on the Sarasvati)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ब्रह्मयोनिभिराकीर्णं जगाम यदुनन्दनः ।\nयत्र दाल्भ्यो बको राजन्पश्वर्थं सुमहातपाः ।\nजुहाव धृतराष्ट्रस्य राष्ट्रं वैचित्रवीर्यिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Yadu's son went to a place crowded with Brahmins, where Baka Dalbhya, king, of great austerity, once made offerings for the sake of animals, to destroy the kingdom of Dhritarashtra, son of Vichitravirya."}},{"n":2,"text":"तपसा घोररूपेण कर्शयन्देहमात्मनः ।\nक्रोधेन महताविष्टो धर्मात्मा वै प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He wasted his body by terrible austerity, seized by great anger, that righteous and mighty one."}},{"n":3,"text":"पुरा हि नैमिषेयाणां सत्रे द्वादशवार्षिके ।\nवृत्ते विश्वजितोऽन्ते वै पाञ्चालानृषयोऽगमन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, in the twelve-year session of the sages of Naimisha, after the Vishvajit sacrifice ended, the sages went to the Panchalas."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्रेश्वरमयाचन्त दक्षिणार्थं मनीषिणः ।\nबलान्वितान्वत्सतरान्निर्व्याधीनेकविंशतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the wise ones asked the ruler for their fee: twenty-one strong, healthy young calves."}},{"n":5,"text":"तानब्रवीद्बको वृद्धो विभजध्वं पशूनिति ।\nपशूनेतानहं त्यक्त्वा भिक्षिष्ये राजसत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The aged Baka said to them: divide the animals among you; I will give up these animals and beg from the best of kings."}},{"n":6,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्नृषीन्सर्वान्प्रतापवान् ।\nजगाम धृतराष्ट्रस्य भवनं ब्राह्मणोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to all the sages, the mighty best of Brahmins went to the house of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":7,"text":"स समीपगतो भूत्वा धृतराष्ट्रं जनेश्वरम् ।\nअयाचत पशून्दाल्भ्यः स चैनं रुषितोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming near to the lord of men Dhritarashtra, Dalbhya asked for animals, and the king, angered, said to him:"}},{"n":8,"text":"यदृच्छया मृता दृष्ट्वा गास्तदा नृपसत्तम ।\nएतान्पशून्नय क्षिप्रं ब्रह्मबन्धो यदीच्छसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, angered, said: best of kings, seeing that cows had chanced to die, take these animals quickly, Brahmin in name only, if you want them."}},{"n":9,"text":"ऋषिस्त्वथ वचः श्रुत्वा चिन्तयामास धर्मवित् ।\nअहो बत नृशंसं वै वाक्यमुक्तोऽस्मि संसदि ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage, hearing the words, knew dharma and thought: alas, a cruel speech has been said to me in the assembly."}},{"n":10,"text":"चिन्तयित्वा मुहूर्तं च रोषाविष्टो द्विजोत्तमः ।\nमतिं चक्रे विनाशाय धृतराष्ट्रस्य भूपतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After brooding a moment, the best of the twice-born, filled with anger, resolved on the destruction of King Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":11,"text":"स उत्कृत्य मृतानां वै मांसानि द्विजसत्तमः ।\nजुहाव धृतराष्ट्रस्य राष्ट्रं नरपतेः पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cutting flesh from the dead cows, that best of Brahmins offered it as oblation against the kingdom of Dhritarashtra."}},{"n":12,"text":"अवकीर्णे सरस्वत्यास्तीर्थे प्रज्वाल्य पावकम् ।\nबको दाल्भ्यो महाराज नियमं परमास्थितः ।\nस तैरेव जुहावास्य राष्ट्रं मांसैर्महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lighting a fire at the Sarasvati's tirtha called Avakirna, Baka Dalbhya, great king, firm in a vow, the greatly austere one, offered the kingdom of Dhritarashtra with that very flesh."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु विधिवत्सत्रे संप्रवृत्ते सुदारुणे ।\nअक्षीयत ततो राष्ट्रं धृतराष्ट्रस्य पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that fearful session was duly under way, the kingdom of Dhritarashtra began to decline, king."}},{"n":14,"text":"छिद्यमानं यथानन्तं वनं परशुना विभो ।\nबभूवापहतं तच्चाप्यवकीर्णमचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a great forest being cut down with an axe, lord, it was ruined, scattered and senseless."}},{"n":15,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तदवकीर्णं तु राष्ट्रं स मनुजाधिपः ।\nबभूव दुर्मना राजंश्चिन्तयामास च प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his kingdom thus ruined, that lord of men became downcast, king, and thought it over."}},{"n":16,"text":"मोक्षार्थमकरोद्यत्नं ब्राह्मणैः सहितः पुरा ।\nअथासौ पार्थिवः खिन्नस्ते च विप्रास्तदा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"He first tried for release with the Brahmins; then that king and those Brahmins were worn out, king."}},{"n":17,"text":"यदा चापि न शक्नोति राष्ट्रं मोचयितुं नृप ।\nअथ वैप्राश्निकांस्तत्र पप्रच्छ जनमेजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he could not free his kingdom, king, Janamejaya, he questioned the Brahmins who answer questions."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो वैप्राश्निकाः प्राहुः पशुविप्रकृतस्त्वया ।\nमांसैरभिजुहोतीति तव राष्ट्रं मुनिर्बकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The questioners said: you have wronged the sage Baka over animals, and he is offering your kingdom with flesh as oblation."}},{"n":19,"text":"तेन ते हूयमानस्य राष्ट्रस्यास्य क्षयो महान् ।\nतस्यैतत्तपसः कर्म येन ते ह्यनयो महान् ।\nअपां कुञ्जे सरस्वत्यास्तं प्रसादय पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because he offers it thus, there is great ruin in your kingdom. This is the work of his austerity, and by it you suffer this great misfortune. Appease him, king, in the Sarasvati's pool of waters."}},{"n":20,"text":"सरस्वतीं ततो गत्वा स राजा बकमब्रवीत् ।\nनिपत्य शिरसा भूमौ प्राञ्जलिर्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king went to the Sarasvati, bowed his head to the ground, hands joined, bull of the Bharatas, and said to Baka:"}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रसादये त्वा भगवन्नपराधं क्षमस्व मे ।\nमम दीनस्य लुब्धस्य मौर्ख्येण हतचेतसः ।\nत्वं गतिस्त्वं च मे नाथः प्रसादं कर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blessed one, I seek to appease you; forgive my offense. I was pitiable and greedy, my mind ruined by folly; you are my refuge and my lord, you should show grace."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं तथा विलपन्तं तु शोकोपहतचेतसम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा तस्य कृपा जज्ञे राष्ट्रं तच्च व्यमोचयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him lament so, his mind struck by grief, compassion arose in the sage, and he released the kingdom."}},{"n":23,"text":"ऋषिः प्रसन्नस्तस्याभूत्संरम्भं च विहाय सः ।\nमोक्षार्थं तस्य राष्ट्रस्य जुहाव पुनराहुतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage became pleased with him, gave up his fury, and offered a fresh oblation to release the kingdom."}},{"n":24,"text":"मोक्षयित्वा ततो राष्ट्रं प्रतिगृह्य पशून्बहून् ।\nहृष्टात्मा नैमिषारण्यं जगाम पुनरेव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having freed the kingdom and received many animals, Baka went happily back to the Naimisha forest."}},{"n":25,"text":"धृतराष्ट्रोऽपि धर्मात्मा स्वस्थचेता महामनाः ।\nस्वमेव नगरं राजा प्रतिपेदे महर्द्धिमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra, righteous and great-minded, his mind at ease, returned to his own very prosperous city."}},{"n":26,"text":"तत्र तीर्थे महाराज बृहस्पतिरुदारधीः ।\nअसुराणामभावाय भावाय च दिवौकसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that tirtha, great king, Brihaspati of noble mind made an offering with flesh, for the destruction of the asuras and the welfare of the gods."}},{"n":27,"text":"मांसैरपि जुहावेष्टिमक्षीयन्त ततोऽसुराः ।\nदैवतैरपि संभग्ना जितकाशिभिराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the asuras were destroyed, shattered in battle even by the gods who were victorious over their foes."}},{"n":28,"text":"तत्रापि विधिवद्दत्त्वा ब्राह्मणेभ्यो महायशाः ।\nवाजिनः कुञ्जरांश्चैव रथांश्चाश्वतरीयुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too Balarama, greatly renowned, duly gave Brahmins horses, elephants, chariots with mules,"}},{"n":29,"text":"रत्नानि च महार्हाणि धनं धान्यं च पुष्कलम् ।\nययौ तीर्थं महाबाहुर्यायातं पृथिवीपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"precious jewels, wealth and abundant grain, and the mighty-armed one went to the tirtha of Yayata, lord of the earth."}},{"n":30,"text":"यत्र यज्ञे ययातेस्तु महाराज सरस्वती ।\nसर्पिः पयश्च सुस्राव नाहुषस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the sacrifice of Yayati there, great king, the Sarasvati flowed with ghee and milk for the great-souled son of Nahusha."}},{"n":31,"text":"तत्रेष्ट्वा पुरुषव्याघ्रो ययातिः पृथिवीपतिः ।\nआक्रामदूर्ध्वं मुदितो लेभे लोकांश्च पुष्कलान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Yayati, tiger among men and lord of the earth, having sacrificed, rose upward joyfully and gained abundant worlds."}},{"n":32,"text":"ययातेर्यजमानस्य यत्र राजन्सरस्वती ।\nप्रसृता प्रददौ कामान्ब्राह्मणानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where the Sarasvati flowed forth for the sacrificing Yayati, king, she granted the wishes of the great-souled Brahmins."}},{"n":33,"text":"यत्र यत्र हि यो विप्रो यान्यान्कामानभीप्सति ।\nतत्र तत्र सरिच्छ्रेष्ठा ससर्ज सुबहून्रसान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever a Brahmin desired any wish, there the best of rivers produced very many savors."}},{"n":34,"text":"तत्र देवाः सगन्धर्वाः प्रीता यज्ञस्य संपदा ।\nविस्मिता मानुषाश्चासन्दृष्ट्वा तां यज्ञसंपदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the gods and gandharvas, pleased with the richness of the sacrifice, and humans too were amazed, seeing that wealth of sacrifice."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततस्तालकेतुर्महाधर्मसेतु-\nर्महात्मा कृतात्मा महादाननित्यः ।\nवसिष्ठापवाहं महाभीमवेगं\nधृतात्मा जितात्मा समभ्याजगाम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the palm-bannered Balarama, great bridge of dharma, great-souled, self-disciplined, constant in great giving, steadfast and master of himself, came to Vasishthapavaha, of tremendous fearful speed."}}]}]}